  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Back in the kitchen, Eleonora reassures the cooks that Viktor Petrovich will recover, but since Lyova sprained his ankle, they have no sous-chef either. Senya and Fedya decline a temporary replacement and immediately clash over who will lead.",
   "gap": 0.8
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Виктор Петрович обязательно скоро поправится.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Только пока без всякой паники.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "У Лёвы сильное растяжение ноги.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Он выбыл примерно на неделю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Я найму временного шефа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Неделю мы как-нибудь сами справимся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Три недели без шефа работали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Мы же все настоящие профессионалы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Я сам приму свежую рыбу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ты теперь тут главный, да?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Ты же совсем безответственный повар.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "У тебя всю кухню разворуют.",
   "gap": 0.9
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "Now let's go back through their conversation line by line and unpack the Russian phrasing.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Виктор Петрович обязательно скоро поправится.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Viktor Petrovich will definitely recover soon.' The grammar packs 'definitely' and 'will recover' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Только пока без всякой паники.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Just no panic at all for now.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'only' before landing on 'panic'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "У Лёвы сильное растяжение ноги.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Lyova has a bad leg sprain.' Eleonora brings out the contrast between 'at' and 'Lyova' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Он выбыл примерно на неделю.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'He is sidelined for about a week.' The meaning hinges on 'he' working together with 'week' in spoken Russian.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Я найму временного шефа.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will hire a temporary chef.' The grammar packs 'I' and 'temporary' into a tight, idiomatic kitchen exchange. Senya answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Неделю мы как-нибудь сами справимся.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'For a week we will manage somehow by ourselves.' Senya brings out the contrast between 'week' and 'we' in a few short words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Три недели без шефа работали.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We worked three weeks without the chef.' In Russian, the idea of 'three' flows naturally into 'worked' without extra filler words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Мы же все настоящие профессионалы.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'We are all true professionals, after all.' Spoken Russian keeps this brisk, leaning on 'we' and finishing on 'professionals'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Я сам приму свежую рыбу.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'I will accept the fresh fish myself.' Notice how Russian expresses 'I' and 'fish' with crisp inflection rather than helper words.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "Ты теперь тут главный, да?",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'Are you the boss in here now, or what?' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'you' before landing on 'yes'.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "eleonora",
   "t": "Ты же совсем безответственный повар.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'You are a completely irresponsible cook.' Notice how Russian expresses 'you' and 'cook' with crisp inflection rather than helper words. Fedya answers right away.",
   "gap": 0.4
  },
  {
   "v": "fedya",
   "t": "У тебя всю кухню разворуют.",
   "gap": 0.55
  },
  {
   "v": "narrator",
   "t": "'They will steal the whole kitchen under you.' Here the Russian phrasing highlights 'at' before landing on 'they will steal everything'. Alright, let's hear the entire conversation one more time from start to finish.",
   "gap": 0.9
